theo-pod (t-169): reject pulse data outside the long window

get_pulse_data() reads pulse_start_sfb (6 bits) and up to four 5-bit
offsets without checking them against the window. pulse_nc() then reads
win_sfb_top[0][pulse_start_sfb - 1] past the scalefactor band table and
writes coefficients past the 1024-line spectrum. getics() now rejects
the frame when pulse_start_sfb >= num_swb or the last pulse falls past
coef_per_frame, as ISO/IEC 14496-3 requires. Found by the host fuzzer (ASan
global-buffer-overflow in pulse_nc); regression input
tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-pulse-outside-window.bin.

